1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,290
[dramatic sound]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:04,300
Lara.

3
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:09,050
Lara?

4
00:00:10,010 --> 00:00:10,680
Lara?

5
00:00:11,430 --> 00:00:12,300
Lara?

6
00:00:13,050 --> 00:00:13,720
Lara?

7
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:16,390
Hey, Lara!

8
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:17,770
Lara.

9
00:00:18,430 --> 00:00:19,270
Lara!

10
00:00:19,770 --> 00:00:20,600
Lara!

11
00:00:23,110 --> 00:00:23,770
Lara...

12
00:00:24,730 --> 00:00:27,240
what is it that you really want?

13
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:34,030
[thud]

14
00:00:37,330 --> 00:00:38,200
[ROWAN] Beautiful.

15
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:43,540
This is how...
you were supposed to be.

16
00:00:44,170 --> 00:00:45,460
[gasps] Father!

17
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:47,760
Are you okay?

18
00:00:48,670 --> 00:00:49,550
Father!

19
00:00:50,470 --> 00:00:52,390
[creaking]

20
00:00:58,390 --> 00:01:00,480
[ROWAN] I used the power
of our royal spear

21
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:04,020
to dispel the evil
curse of that potion.

22
00:01:06,020 --> 00:01:08,280
Having the legs of those
hideous humans

23
00:01:08,990 --> 00:01:10,990
will twist the light and
cloud your eyes,

24
00:01:11,070 --> 00:01:12,410
making you forget who you are.

25
00:01:13,530 --> 00:01:14,950
-What are you-—
-Now is the time.

26
00:01:15,030 --> 00:01:16,950
Fulfill your destiny
as a princess.

27
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:19,250
You have to use your blade.

28
00:01:19,950 --> 00:01:21,750
Use it to pierce your
loved one with it.

29
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:25,130
You must purify the light,
and then those hideous

30
00:01:25,210 --> 00:01:27,050
- humans will fight-—
- But why?

31
00:01:28,750 --> 00:01:30,220
You don't need to know why.

32
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:32,130
[rumbling]

33
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:34,180
[gasps]

34
00:01:35,390 --> 00:01:37,560
No, it's falling apart!

35
00:01:38,810 --> 00:01:41,060
- Lara, you have to save Father!
- [gasps]

36
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:45,440
Where am I?

37
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:47,520
[helicopter whirring]

38
00:01:47,610 --> 00:01:49,230
[magical sound]

39
00:01:50,530 --> 00:01:52,360
Ever since a new species
of aquatic plant

40
00:01:52,450 --> 00:01:54,860
was spotted in Lake Biwa,
Shiga Prefecture, this month,

41
00:01:54,950 --> 00:01:57,580
there have been reports
of unidentified microorganisms

42
00:01:57,660 --> 00:01:59,660
and ecosystem disruptions.
[phone vibrating]

43
00:02:00,290 --> 00:02:02,120
[YOSHIYA] Dad, can you hear me?
It's Mari.

44
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:03,670
Mari's in trouble.

45
00:02:05,210 --> 00:02:07,710
It's the boat. We're looking,
but we can't find her anywhere.

46
00:02:08,420 --> 00:02:09,420
-Mari.
- Calling around-—

47
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:11,130
Kota!

48
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:14,180
The place-— it's crumbling.

49
00:02:15,430 --> 00:02:17,350
The witch's power
is beginning to fade,

50
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:20,390
but Father is also losing
his strength by the minute.

51
00:02:21,390 --> 00:02:22,520
We're running out of time.

52
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:25,400
[sighs]

53
00:02:27,230 --> 00:02:30,190
[underwater sounds]

54
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:42,750
No,

55
00:02:43,460 --> 00:02:44,710
I can't go back anywhere.

56
00:02:46,170 --> 00:02:47,540
Not even to the surface.

57
00:02:48,250 --> 00:02:49,170
Nowhere.

58
00:02:51,420 --> 00:02:52,550
Why would you say that?

59
00:02:53,420 --> 00:02:54,300
Why, Father?

60
00:02:55,260 --> 00:02:56,130
It isn't fair.

61
00:02:56,550 --> 00:02:58,260
Humans aren't hideous at all.

62
00:02:59,350 --> 00:03:01,350
The time I spent
with them all gave me

63
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:04,100
is something irreplaceable.

64
00:03:04,850 --> 00:03:06,350
So I could never do it.

65
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:08,100
Stab someone I love?

66
00:03:09,730 --> 00:03:10,560
There's no way.

67
00:03:11,270 --> 00:03:12,110
No way.

68
00:03:13,490 --> 00:03:14,360
[LUNA] Lara?

69
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:17,990
[gasps]

70
00:03:18,490 --> 00:03:19,700
I think I can hear...

71
00:03:20,780 --> 00:03:21,780
Lara's voice.

72
00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:24,620
-Luna!
-I can hear it.

73
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:26,710
The voice...

74
00:03:27,670 --> 00:03:29,330
of the Princess of Light.

75
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:31,670
Yes, that's it.

76
00:03:32,670 --> 00:03:34,300
The voice of our beloved sister.

77
00:03:35,220 --> 00:03:37,510
Lara, give us light.

78
00:03:38,630 --> 00:03:39,470
You can do it.

79
00:03:40,430 --> 00:03:41,300
I know you can.

80
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:43,640
Do it for us.

81
00:03:46,140 --> 00:03:47,690
So then, this time,

82
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:50,310
pierce right through them.

83
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:52,440
Pierce straight through the
souls of humans.

84
00:03:53,650 --> 00:03:56,280
Through the hearts of those
hideous human beings.

85
00:03:56,860 --> 00:04:00,030
-I hate them.
-I hate every single human.

86
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:03,120
They stole the light
from all of us.

87
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:06,500
They took your love for
granted and betrayed you.

88
00:04:07,210 --> 00:04:09,540
I hate humans so much.

89
00:04:11,210 --> 00:04:13,590
And so do you, deep down.

90
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:17,670
Even now, because that hatred
won't fade away.

91
00:04:20,430 --> 00:04:23,720
And because you've
been crying all this time.

92
00:04:24,220 --> 00:04:26,390
[underwater sounds]

93
00:04:31,730 --> 00:04:33,690
[♪ opening music begins]

94
00:05:20,110 --> 00:05:22,030
EDITING AND TYPESETTING:
ASHLEY BARBOZA

95
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:59,190
[♪ opening music ends]

96
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:04,740
[Lisa sobs]

97
00:06:06,410 --> 00:06:07,450
[footsteps]

98
00:06:10,450 --> 00:06:11,290
It's you.

99
00:06:11,830 --> 00:06:13,290
Just what are you doing here?

100
00:06:13,830 --> 00:06:15,290
-[MARI] Is he okay?
-Stop.

101
00:06:17,630 --> 00:06:18,460
Why are you here?

102
00:06:19,750 --> 00:06:22,130
I have to see Lara.
I want to help her.

103
00:06:23,840 --> 00:06:25,090
So she called you then?

104
00:06:26,300 --> 00:06:27,640
[MARI] She told me
not to come here,

105
00:06:28,470 --> 00:06:29,390
but...

106
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:32,310
[helicopter whirring]

107
00:06:40,690 --> 00:06:42,610
Lara is over there,

108
00:06:43,740 --> 00:06:45,320
in the place shrouded in fog.

109
00:06:47,120 --> 00:06:49,490
If you want to see her,
just walk that way.

110
00:06:53,790 --> 00:06:54,660
Go on.

111
00:06:57,630 --> 00:06:58,500
Thank you.

112
00:07:12,010 --> 00:07:12,680
You'll die.

113
00:07:14,390 --> 00:07:17,310
If you go to that
place... you will die.

114
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:22,570
You can't see that blade,
can you? There in the sky.

115
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:25,110
-[MARI] A blade?
-[LISA] That's right.

116
00:07:25,690 --> 00:07:27,700
It's Lara's actual heart
floating in midair.

117
00:07:29,030 --> 00:07:29,740
You can't see it.

118
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:32,540
After all, you're only human.

119
00:07:33,750 --> 00:07:34,700
The true light...

120
00:07:35,750 --> 00:07:37,210
is invisible to humans.

121
00:07:38,710 --> 00:07:42,210
Mermaids and humans, we both
came from the same sea once.

122
00:07:43,460 --> 00:07:46,420
However, you humans chose
to close your eyes

123
00:07:47,760 --> 00:07:50,470
until... you couldn't
see anything at all.

124
00:07:55,140 --> 00:07:57,560
You're just a mere human!
You don't know!

125
00:07:58,480 --> 00:08:00,900
You can't possibly understand
Lara or any of us!

126
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:03,610
Us mermaids, we're
noble beings of light!

127
00:08:04,190 --> 00:08:05,150
But you!

128
00:08:06,110 --> 00:08:08,070
You turned your backs on
the light and on true love!

129
00:08:08,700 --> 00:08:11,120
There's no way you can begin
to understand her!

130
00:08:15,410 --> 00:08:17,250
[MARI] I can't see
into Lara's heart,

131
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:18,580
and so I have to get closer.

132
00:08:20,630 --> 00:08:21,960
That is why I have to go

133
00:08:24,210 --> 00:08:25,050
and be with her.

134
00:08:29,130 --> 00:08:32,100
[KOTA] I don't want Lady
Lara to have to kill...

135
00:08:33,510 --> 00:08:35,760
someone who she loves dearly.

136
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:38,060
[Lisa sobs]

137
00:08:38,140 --> 00:08:41,350
Because I also... have
someone... I love too.

138
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:43,020
[Lisa cries]

139
00:08:44,110 --> 00:08:44,980
I hate...

140
00:08:47,280 --> 00:08:48,400
those humans.

141
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:52,320
[bubbling]

142
00:08:54,780 --> 00:08:56,290
[phone buzzes]
Ah! Mari?

143
00:08:56,750 --> 00:08:58,250
Hey, Mari, is that you?

144
00:08:59,790 --> 00:09:03,460
-Can you hear me, big bro?
-Yeah, but I don't understand.

145
00:09:03,540 --> 00:09:05,960
- Where are you right now?
-Fukushima.

146
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:08,300
Huh? Why are you there?

147
00:09:08,380 --> 00:09:11,010
I'm sorry, signal is
really weak here.

148
00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:14,600
You idiot! Don't you know
it's total chaos here?

149
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:17,260
I'm sorry, but it'll be okay.

150
00:09:18,640 --> 00:09:21,310
-I'll be back once I get Lara.
-Uh, wait, Lara's there too?

151
00:09:21,390 --> 00:09:23,690
Lara! Hey, Mari, is Lara there?

152
00:09:24,520 --> 00:09:26,270
-Yeah, she's here.
-Oh! Okay, great.

153
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:28,440
-I'm heading there now.
-You can't.

154
00:09:28,530 --> 00:09:30,990
What are you talking about?
Look...

155
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:33,360
I hurt Lara and I feel

156
00:09:33,450 --> 00:09:35,030
responsible for that.

157
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:37,240
Please, I just want to help
out in any way I can.

158
00:09:40,460 --> 00:09:43,040
All right, why don't you
tell her about yourself

159
00:09:43,920 --> 00:09:46,000
later today when
they bring her home?

160
00:09:47,340 --> 00:09:49,210
-[gasps]
- Thank you, Mari.

161
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:59,430
- [MARI] Lara?
- Uh? Mari.

162
00:10:00,350 --> 00:10:02,140
-Lara!
-[LARA] You shouldn't be here!

163
00:10:03,350 --> 00:10:04,230
Stay away,

164
00:10:05,190 --> 00:10:05,980
otherwise...

165
00:10:06,860 --> 00:10:08,690
- I might kill you.
- [gasps]

166
00:10:12,150 --> 00:10:13,030
Lara...

167
00:10:20,370 --> 00:10:23,370
[LARA] I guess in the end
I never found true love.

168
00:10:25,170 --> 00:10:26,670
I suppose after all,
I'm a mermaid...

169
00:10:27,630 --> 00:10:28,710
and you're all human.

170
00:10:30,300 --> 00:10:32,220
I tried to ignore that truth...

171
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:36,130
but it grew within me
during my 200-year sleep.

172
00:10:37,180 --> 00:10:38,550
It was a hatred so intense,

173
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:41,310
I'm frightened to
even think about it.

174
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:45,520
I can't erase this turmoil
in my heart. It won't go.

175
00:10:46,770 --> 00:10:48,770
So as long as this hatred
remains within us,

176
00:10:50,190 --> 00:10:52,360
the only fate awaiting
mermaids and humans

177
00:10:53,150 --> 00:10:54,400
is to devour one another.

178
00:10:57,450 --> 00:11:00,160
So then, this princess
must vanish...

179
00:11:01,660 --> 00:11:03,250
so that no one else gets hurt.

180
00:11:04,660 --> 00:11:06,250
I will put an end to this fate.

181
00:11:09,170 --> 00:11:11,040
Have you forgotten
the promise we made?

182
00:11:12,460 --> 00:11:13,590
We promised each other

183
00:11:14,510 --> 00:11:15,720
I would become a pro boxer

184
00:11:16,510 --> 00:11:18,430
and you would make
me a delicious giant cake.

185
00:11:20,350 --> 00:11:23,640
That's enough. You
and I are totally different.

186
00:11:24,980 --> 00:11:27,600
We see different things.
We live in different worlds.

187
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:29,310
Stay away!

188
00:11:30,020 --> 00:11:33,360
Please, please,
don't come any closer!

189
00:11:34,070 --> 00:11:36,400
It's useless, you and I,
a mermaid and a human.

190
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:38,740
We're completely
different beings.

191
00:11:39,660 --> 00:11:42,490
[♪ dramatic music]

192
00:11:42,580 --> 00:11:45,330
[MARI] Yeah, we are
completely different.

193
00:11:47,410 --> 00:11:50,290
I mean, you're an idiot,
you're annoying,

194
00:11:51,380 --> 00:11:52,750
you're always getting in my way.

195
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:54,630
But that's why...

196
00:11:56,470 --> 00:11:59,430
when I'm with you,
I no longer feel alone.

197
00:12:00,180 --> 00:12:02,390
[♪ dramatic music]

198
00:12:02,470 --> 00:12:03,640
I don't care about fate.

199
00:12:06,430 --> 00:12:10,690
Lara... weren't you-—
weren't we both...

200
00:12:13,190 --> 00:12:14,400
born to love somebody,

201
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:16,570
no matter who or why?

202
00:12:19,990 --> 00:12:21,200
[piercing sound]

203
00:12:40,720 --> 00:12:42,640
[helicopter whirring]

204
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:47,600
Mari?

205
00:12:48,480 --> 00:12:49,270
Mari?

206
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:50,520
Mari!

207
00:12:50,890 --> 00:12:53,110
[helicopter whirring]

208
00:12:54,020 --> 00:12:55,650
[LARA] Mari!
Mari!

209
00:12:57,530 --> 00:12:59,700
Mari!
No, wake up!

210
00:13:00,570 --> 00:13:03,120
Mari!
Please, Mari!

211
00:13:04,330 --> 00:13:05,240
No!

212
00:13:08,710 --> 00:13:11,040
[high-pitched chime]

213
00:13:19,630 --> 00:13:20,550
The light.

214
00:13:23,260 --> 00:13:25,470
The light of the one...
I love.

215
00:13:27,510 --> 00:13:30,560
I have...
always wanted it.

216
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:33,350
The light.

217
00:13:36,270 --> 00:13:39,280
[RIGMOR] What was it
that you really wanted?

218
00:13:40,780 --> 00:13:42,530
[GRACE] What did
you really need,

219
00:13:43,570 --> 00:13:44,530
Lara?

220
00:13:46,740 --> 00:13:49,080
[grunts]

221
00:13:49,700 --> 00:13:52,580
No! Shut up!
I don't need anything!

222
00:13:53,290 --> 00:13:55,130
It would've been fine
if I just disappeared!

223
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,630
Don't care at all
what happens to me,

224
00:13:58,420 --> 00:14:00,170
but you have to stay
here in this world!

225
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:03,550
[intense rumbling]

226
00:14:04,590 --> 00:14:05,470
Mari...

227
00:14:06,430 --> 00:14:07,260
Mari...

228
00:14:08,220 --> 00:14:09,100
Mari...

229
00:14:10,270 --> 00:14:12,480
[underwater rumbling]

230
00:14:13,940 --> 00:14:16,110
Mari...
[gasps]

231
00:14:20,400 --> 00:14:22,280
[piercing sound]
[Lara screams]

232
00:14:22,700 --> 00:14:23,780
It hurts!
[slash]

233
00:14:25,030 --> 00:14:27,120
It hurts!
[slash]

234
00:14:27,950 --> 00:14:29,620
It hurts!
[slash]

235
00:14:30,540 --> 00:14:31,410
It hurts!

236
00:14:32,120 --> 00:14:33,620
It hurts!
[slash]

237
00:14:40,130 --> 00:14:41,130
[LARA] I can't move.

238
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:42,630
[slash]

239
00:14:46,340 --> 00:14:47,680
[LARA] I'm not able to save you.

240
00:14:48,800 --> 00:14:49,640
[slash]

241
00:14:51,720 --> 00:14:54,270
[LARA] Is this it?
Is this what happens?

242
00:14:55,480 --> 00:14:57,770
The fate that awaits
mermaids and humans?

243
00:15:00,190 --> 00:15:01,190
I really wish...

244
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:04,320
I hadn't come back to life.

245
00:15:08,320 --> 00:15:09,200
Lara?

246
00:15:14,410 --> 00:15:15,290
No.

247
00:15:16,250 --> 00:15:17,080
No!

248
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:19,670
I'm glad I came back to life!

249
00:15:20,340 --> 00:15:22,300
I'm glad I got to come
back to the surface!

250
00:15:23,170 --> 00:15:26,340
Even now, I'm still glad of
everything! I've no regrets!

251
00:15:27,430 --> 00:15:29,010
That's just who I am.

252
00:15:29,640 --> 00:15:30,600
I am-—

253
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:33,220
I'm clumsy, a nuisance,

254
00:15:33,890 --> 00:15:36,230
a total idiot of a mermaid.

255
00:15:37,190 --> 00:15:38,650
But so what if I'm an idiot?

256
00:15:40,190 --> 00:15:41,440
So what if that's who I am?

257
00:15:42,110 --> 00:15:43,320
Don't underestimate me!

258
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:46,360
It's a lie that I'd rather
just disappear.

259
00:15:47,610 --> 00:15:50,530
Even...
if I had to stay in this form,

260
00:15:51,490 --> 00:15:53,160
I'd still want to
stay in this world.

261
00:15:55,660 --> 00:15:59,210
Because of this world...
you're here.

262
00:15:59,630 --> 00:16:00,710
[energy humming]

263
00:16:01,210 --> 00:16:02,130
I,

264
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:03,960
I...

265
00:16:05,050 --> 00:16:05,970
I...

266
00:16:08,340 --> 00:16:11,260
I'm supposed to find real
love, but I don't want it.

267
00:16:11,350 --> 00:16:12,720
[chimes]
[flaking]

268
00:16:14,060 --> 00:16:14,930
All I want,

269
00:16:15,020 --> 00:16:16,560
[♪ soft music]

270
00:16:17,350 --> 00:16:18,350
[magical sound]

271
00:16:18,690 --> 00:16:19,520
All I want...

272
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:26,650
is to be alive in a world
where-— you're here.

273
00:16:27,450 --> 00:16:30,280
[♪ soft music continues]

274
00:16:45,300 --> 00:16:48,260
[♪ soft music continues]

275
00:16:53,720 --> 00:16:55,140
[chimes]

276
00:16:58,270 --> 00:16:59,140
[gasps]

277
00:16:59,230 --> 00:17:00,270
[chimes]

278
00:17:03,650 --> 00:17:06,610
[♪ soft music continues]

279
00:17:12,410 --> 00:17:13,620
[chimes]

280
00:17:16,370 --> 00:17:18,330
[YOSHI] Oh man,
my dad's gonna kill me.

281
00:17:18,410 --> 00:17:19,450
I just know it.

282
00:17:21,710 --> 00:17:23,040
What are you looking at?

283
00:17:23,830 --> 00:17:26,750
[LUCA] The sky...
it just flashed.

284
00:17:27,300 --> 00:17:28,210
Uh?

285
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:30,510
[water splashes]

286
00:17:36,390 --> 00:17:38,930
[MARI] So did I just
die or something?

287
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:41,730
-[LARA] Yes.
-[MARI] Hmm...

288
00:17:42,730 --> 00:17:44,310
[LARA] What do you mean "hmm"?

289
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:47,400
Well, I came back
to life after dying.

290
00:17:48,110 --> 00:17:50,190
I guess that really does
make me the strongest.

291
00:17:51,110 --> 00:17:51,780
I guess.

292
00:17:53,700 --> 00:17:55,320
-Mari.
-Hmm?

293
00:17:56,580 --> 00:17:58,660
So I think the entire time...

294
00:18:00,410 --> 00:18:01,710
I was searching for something.

295
00:18:03,580 --> 00:18:06,000
I was searching for
a world to live in

296
00:18:07,380 --> 00:18:08,340
all along.

297
00:18:09,510 --> 00:18:11,260
[magical sound]

298
00:18:14,470 --> 00:18:16,180
It's been 6 months

299
00:18:16,260 --> 00:18:17,680
since the phenomenon occurred
in Lake Biwa.

300
00:18:18,390 --> 00:18:20,520
Water quality data has
returned to normal levels,

301
00:18:20,600 --> 00:18:23,270
and the excessive
proliferation of phytoplankton

302
00:18:23,350 --> 00:18:24,690
has now largely subsided.

303
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:28,020
Although Lake Biwa is
gradually returning to normal,

304
00:18:28,110 --> 00:18:30,480
experts are unsure as
to what exactly happened.

305
00:18:30,570 --> 00:18:33,650
[LISA] I wonder, did you
actually find true love?

306
00:18:36,370 --> 00:18:38,950
The light that you found...
it's so different

307
00:18:39,040 --> 00:18:40,700
from anything
we've known until now.

308
00:18:41,950 --> 00:18:44,370
However, Father and
all of the others,

309
00:18:44,460 --> 00:18:46,710
they've begun to regain
their power once again.

310
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:50,210
They'll all fully
wake up someday,

311
00:18:50,880 --> 00:18:53,340
whether it's in a year
or even 10 years from now.

312
00:18:55,380 --> 00:18:56,220
But when they do,

313
00:18:57,600 --> 00:19:01,100
their hatred towards humans
won't fade. It never will.

314
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:05,060
[LARA] Even so, I'll reach out
and talk to Father

315
00:19:05,140 --> 00:19:08,520
and the others over and over,
as long as it takes.

316
00:19:09,770 --> 00:19:12,150
I'll talk about the future of
mermaids and humans

317
00:19:12,780 --> 00:19:16,070
because I'm sure that's the
specific light I have found.

318
00:19:16,490 --> 00:19:18,120
[♪ soft piano music]

319
00:19:18,530 --> 00:19:19,410
[sighs]

320
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:22,660
I couldn't admit it
for a long time

321
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:27,500
that I was actually
afraid of you.

322
00:19:30,170 --> 00:19:32,250
I was afraid of the way
you were changing.

323
00:19:33,300 --> 00:19:35,090
But... now...

324
00:19:36,130 --> 00:19:39,180
I want you to hold on to this
for now and in the future.

325
00:19:42,010 --> 00:19:42,680
Thank you.

326
00:19:45,180 --> 00:19:48,100
[♪ soft piano music continues]

327
00:19:51,820 --> 00:19:54,730
[LUCA] You know, you're
always so impulsive, Lara.

328
00:19:54,820 --> 00:19:57,490
- [LARA] Impulsive?
- You show up out of the blue,

329
00:19:57,570 --> 00:19:59,370
and then just as
quick you disappear.

330
00:20:00,030 --> 00:20:01,240
I guess that's true.

331
00:20:01,330 --> 00:20:03,700
Like, you had that urge
to want to date me,

332
00:20:04,410 --> 00:20:06,040
and suddenly
wanting to break up.

333
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:08,460
-It kind of hurt.
-I'm sorry.

334
00:20:09,630 --> 00:20:11,210
Try to see it from
my perspective.

335
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,000
I'm really sorry.

336
00:20:14,340 --> 00:20:16,210
Now, the world's open,
where will you go?

337
00:20:17,670 --> 00:20:18,550
Let's see,

338
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:21,350
I guess I'll head to where

339
00:20:22,220 --> 00:20:23,600
a new light is waiting.

340
00:20:25,930 --> 00:20:29,310
Lara! I forgot to say,
I finished your portrait.

341
00:20:30,650 --> 00:20:31,690
Come see it sometime.

342
00:20:34,820 --> 00:20:36,820
So you didn't repaint it?

343
00:20:38,740 --> 00:20:41,620
Idiot! You'd actually be shocked
if you saw it.

344
00:20:43,120 --> 00:20:44,200
It's a masterpiece.

345
00:20:48,910 --> 00:20:50,500
[YOSHI] Man, I'm so lonely.

346
00:20:50,580 --> 00:20:52,630
Just how long are
you going to sulk for?

347
00:20:52,710 --> 00:20:53,670
[YOSHI] I'm not sulking.

348
00:20:54,500 --> 00:20:55,840
Lara, walk you to the station?

349
00:20:56,960 --> 00:20:59,590
Oh, thank you, but I'm going
shopping with Mari first.

350
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:01,470
- Huh?
- Don't forget you've

351
00:21:01,550 --> 00:21:04,180
- got a shift later on.
- Take care.

352
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:06,680
All right, now don't be
a stranger.

353
00:21:07,390 --> 00:21:10,520
That's right. Come back
anytime, Lara. Okay?

354
00:21:18,530 --> 00:21:21,530
-I'm already hungry again.
-Didn't you eat enough food?

355
00:21:22,660 --> 00:21:24,740
I've been adding more to my
workout routine lately.

356
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:26,120
Oh?

357
00:21:26,580 --> 00:21:28,290
I've got a tough
session later today.

358
00:21:28,660 --> 00:21:30,290
Just don't overdo it, okay?

359
00:21:30,370 --> 00:21:31,620
I should tell you that.

360
00:21:35,210 --> 00:21:36,800
Do you think you can
live on your own?

361
00:21:38,050 --> 00:21:38,710
Of course I can.

362
00:21:39,510 --> 00:21:41,130
-[MARI] Are you sure?
-[LARA] I'm sure.

363
00:21:41,970 --> 00:21:42,970
The train now arrivi-—

364
00:21:43,050 --> 00:21:44,640
You'll probably
mess something up.

365
00:21:45,220 --> 00:21:46,140
Probably.

366
00:21:48,140 --> 00:21:49,310
Platform one-—

367
00:21:49,390 --> 00:21:50,810
You won't be back
for a while, huh?

368
00:21:52,060 --> 00:21:52,730
Mm-mm.

369
00:21:53,650 --> 00:21:55,230
Please step behind
the yellow line.

370
00:21:57,270 --> 00:21:58,150
[MARI] So then

371
00:21:58,940 --> 00:22:00,940
all that embarrassing
stuff you were saying

372
00:22:01,030 --> 00:22:03,030
about wanting to go
with me or whatever.

373
00:22:03,910 --> 00:22:07,080
-[LARA] Yes, it's true.
-So then why are you leaving?

374
00:22:11,080 --> 00:22:11,750
I'll be...

375
00:22:13,080 --> 00:22:14,080
so lonely.

376
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:18,670
[Mari cries]

377
00:22:26,260 --> 00:22:27,100
Mari.

378
00:22:28,310 --> 00:22:31,310
[train braking]

379
00:22:33,770 --> 00:22:36,730
The train just arrived at
platform 1. It's the 10:50

380
00:22:36,810 --> 00:22:39,280
service bound for
Kobe via Kakogawa.

381
00:22:42,240 --> 00:22:43,360
- [gasps]
-I'm okay.

382
00:22:46,280 --> 00:22:48,620
Are your legs still hurting you?

383
00:22:51,410 --> 00:22:52,290
Mm-hmm.

384
00:22:53,160 --> 00:22:54,250
- But...
- [sighs]

385
00:22:58,710 --> 00:23:00,300
these wounds are who I am,

386
00:23:01,300 --> 00:23:03,970
and so I'll keep walking

387
00:23:05,260 --> 00:23:07,470
on these feet from this day on.

388
00:23:12,470 --> 00:23:13,640
[door closing]

389
00:23:26,650 --> 00:23:29,280
[panting]

390
00:23:40,130 --> 00:23:42,170
[continues panting]
